{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["The word <b>תביאו.</b> is punctuated with a dagesh in the alef, for we do not know its reason." "<b>ממושבתיכם.</b> We require a tradition from what place it is taken and when it is sought." "<b>לחם תנופה.</b> For the priest, with the lambs of the wave-offering."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "Reading זרה as a noun meaning 'punctuation mark'; the logic of the argument is compressed and the point about the alef dagesh is left unexplained as in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:54.389117911Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}